| `∉` asks the opposite of `∈`, and is exactly `not (x ∈ Name)` — one
| character, the way `≠` is one character to `=`'s one. Spelled out it read
| badly: `not` binds looser than `∈`, so `not r ∈ Exception` makes the eye
| work out that the membership is what is negated, not `r`.
emit Length { value = 5 } to core get bad
assert bad ∈ Exception
assert not bad ∉ Exception

emit Length { value = [1, 2] } to core get good
assert good ∉ Exception
assert good.value = 2

| Kinds too, since `∈` answers about both.
assert 3 ∉ String
assert "a" ∉ Number
assert null ∉ Number
assert null ∈ Null

| The everyday shape: carry on only when the emit worked.
if good ∉ Exception
    assert good._class = "LengthResult"
